{
  "sim_type": "excel",
  "title": "Build Titan's Football Field valuation synthesis chart",
  "scenario": "You're a Titan equity analyst on the Mumbai desk. Your DCF, trading comps, and precedent transaction models have produced wildly different valuations: ₹776, ₹3,701, and ₹4,529 respectively. Your PM wants one price target by close of day, backed by a football field chart that shows where the methods agree. You'll construct the valuation ranges, triangulate the consensus zone, and synthesize a defensible target.",
  "instructions": "Build Titan's football field by anchoring each valuation method's low-to-high range, identifying the consensus zone where the most relevant methods overlap, and deriving a price target that balances all evidence. Use formulas to compute per-share values, consensus overlaps, and upside calculations.",
  "learning_objective": "Synthesize four independent valuation methods into a single defensible price target by constructing overlapping ranges, identifying the consensus zone, and weighting methods by relevance to the company.",
  "hints": [
    "Start by calculating the equity value (enterprise value minus net debt) and divide by shares outstanding to convert each method's range into per-share bands.",
    "The consensus zone is where the most relevant methods' ranges overlap—identify the highest low-end and the lowest high-end of those overlapping bands.",
    "Use MAX() for the consensus zone's lower bound and MIN() for its upper bound, then place your target as a weighted position within that zone."
  ],
